tor $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRound the answer to $2$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186369720 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "70bc7c7a-169e-56f1-a44c-50b8995c4794" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369720 #edb/ref 1074 "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {(\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$\n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {\\text{proj}}_{S}x}{‖x‖‖{\\text{proj}}_{S}x‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 3+0\\cdot (-1)}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{13}\\sqrt{11}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{\\sqrt{13}})≈{23.09}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186369721 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369721 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369721 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369721 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369721 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369721 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369721 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369721 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186369726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369721 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a372a12b-f02d-574b-85c9-6ebecf5009c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369722 #edb/ref 1080 "{21.99}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369722 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369722 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b1cac70a-4767-5747-aabc-96ad22e5a366" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369723 #edb/ref 1080 "{19.17}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369723 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369723 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e2ed8d05-f3ce-5e8b-8a39-f7d70814de29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369724 #edb/ref 1080 "{20.77}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369724 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369724 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b1b8838-9e4f-5164-8943-3378b0c8d03b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369